    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4bdde6cc-341f-5934-8614-b15ae7ed0a09",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_S f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y,z)=2 x + y + z$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle - u + 2 v, 3 v + 2, 2 u + v\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 3$ and $0\\le v\\le 3$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|=\\sqrt{70}$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a scalar surface integral, use\n\n$$\n\\iint_S f\\,\\mathrm{d}S=\\iint_D f(\\mathbf r(u,v))\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe supplied area factor is $\\sqrt{70}$.\n\nSubstitute the coordinates and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(\\mathbf r(u,v))&=2 \\left(- u + 2 v\\right) + \\left(3 v + 2\\right) + \\left(2 u + v\\right) \\\\\n&=8 v + 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate over the parameter rectangle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_S f\\,\\mathrm{d}S&=\\sqrt{70}\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(8 v + 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\\n&=\\sqrt{70}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left[u \\left(8 v + 2\\right)\\right]_{u=0}^{u=3}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\\n&=\\sqrt{70}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(24 v + 6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\\n&=\\sqrt{70}\\left[12 v^{2} + 6 v\\right]_{v=0}^{v=3} \\\\\n&=\\sqrt{70}\\left(\\left(126\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\\n&=126 \\sqrt{70}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
