      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_S f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y,z)=x + 2 y - z$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle u - v, 2 u + 2 v, 2 v\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $-2\\le u\\le -1$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|=6$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a scalar surface integral, use\n\n$$\n\\iint_S f\\,\\mathrm{d}S=\\iint_D f(\\mathbf r(u,v))\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe supplied area factor is $6$.\n\nSubstitute the coordinates and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(\\mathbf r(u,v))&=\\left(u - v\\right) + 2 \\left(2 u + 2 v\\right) - \\left(2 v\\right) \\\\\n&=5 u + v.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate over the parameter rectangle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_S f\\,\\mathrm{d}S&=6\\int_{-1}^{1}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\left(5 u + v\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\\n&=6\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left[\\frac{5 u^{2}}{2} + u v\\right]_{u=-2}^{u=-1}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\\n&=6\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(v - \\frac{15}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\\n&=6\\left[\\frac{v^{2}}{2} - \\frac{15 v}{2}\\right]_{v=-1}^{v=1} \\\\\n&=6\\left(\\left(-7\\right)-\\left(8\\right)\\right) \\\\\n&=-90.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
